     "label": "Low pressure, low temperature"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "a",
   "hint": "You want the molecules far apart and fast.",
   "explain": "Low pressure keeps molecules far apart; high temperature makes them move so fast that attractions hardly matter."
  }
 ],
 "takeaways": [
